    "rawText": "[Song Title: Off by One, Still True]\r\n[Style: math rock, polyrhythmic, odd meter, changing meter, clean studio recording, phasing morphing effects guitars, elastic bass, dynamic live drums, expressive grounded male vocal]\r\n[Caption: Almost right can still be right.]\r\n[Image: A ruler slightly misaligned.]\r\n[Refresh Title: Random 4]\r\n[Theme: Random]\r\n[Gradients: 4]\r\n[Rank: 28]\r\n[Title Rarity: 1.94]\r\n[Seeds: 713, A:40, B:4, C:24, D:2]\r\n[Perspective: observer]\r\n[Concept: Imperfect alignment reveals deeper order.]\r\n[Topic: Complexity & Emergence → recursion_and_return]\r\n[Genre Bias: math_rock]\r\n[Style Change: none]\r\n[Modulation: none]\r\n[Hook Prominence: low]\r\n[Deviation: structural bend]\r\n[Created: January 29, 2026 at 9:03 AM]\r\n[Composer Version: v2.3]\r\n\r\n[Intro]\r\n[Guitars strike syncopated chords that never quite repeat.]\r\n[Motif shifts length each cycle.]\r\n\r\n[Verse]\r\n[Drums pivot between tight and loose accents.]\r\nI missed the mark by just a beat  \r\nStill landed somewhere on my feet  \r\nThe answer wasn’t what I planned  \r\nBut fit the question better than\r\n\r\n[Verse]\r\n[Bass climbs while guitars descend.]\r\nEvery loop returns misread  \r\nA clearer truth inside instead  \r\nNot broken, just a shade askew  \r\nEnough to show another view\r\n\r\n[Chorus]\r\n[Brief unison hit, then release.]\r\nOff by one, still true  \r\nThe math holds even when it moves  \r\nWhat looks wrong from far away  \r\nLocks in close enough to stay\r\n\r\n[Verse]\r\n[Guitar tapping grows denser, drums busier.]\r\nPerfection stalls, it wants control  \r\nNear-miss keeps the system whole  \r\nEvery flaw that doesn’t fail  \r\nIs a signal, not a tale\r\n\r\n[Bridge]\r\n[Dropout Before Final: bass alone, then drums creep back.]\r\nIf it lined up flawlessly  \r\nThere’d be nothing left to see  \r\nThe offset keeps the pulse alive  \r\nGives the reason room to drive\r\n\r\n[Final Chorus]\r\n[Full band, tighter phrasing.]\r\